# What the image build must not see.
#
# The `.env*` exclusions are the load-bearing ones. Vite reads `.env`,
# `.env.local` and `.env.production` from the project directory during
# `vite build`, and all three exist here with local values: `.env.local` sets
# VITE_APP_ENV=development and `.env.production` names an example.com host.
# Any of them reaching the build context makes the bundle depend on which
# developer's working copy it was built from. Excluded, the build depends only
# on the build arguments and the defaults in src/config/env.ts.
node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local screenshot captures and bundle audits.
.shots
stats.html
